From: Pyro project
Subject: [PATCH] fs/afs: Fix double-indirect reads

In AFS mode the inode's max_*_range fields count blocks, not bytes, so
every comparison against them in read_bfs_file() shifts by RANGE_SHIFT.
The double-indirect branch subtracts max_indirect_range unshifted, so the
offset into the double-indirect area is off by a factor of the block
size, l1n points past the level-1 table and every read beyond the
indirect range fails with "incorrect double-indirect block".

BFS is unaffected (RANGE_SHIFT is 0 there).

Reproduced with grub-fstest on an AFS image written by Syllable's own AFS
code (two 40 MB files interleaved in 4 KiB chunks): cmp failed at the
first byte past the indirect range before the fix and matches after it.

---
--- a/grub-core/fs/bfs.c
+++ b/grub-core/fs/bfs.c
@@ -350,7 +350,7 @@
 	grub_size_t read_size;
 	grub_off_t double_indirect_offset;
 	double_indirect_offset = off
-	  - grub_bfs_to_cpu64 (ino->max_indirect_range);
+	  - (grub_bfs_to_cpu64 (ino->max_indirect_range) << RANGE_SHIFT);
 	boff = (double_indirect_offset
 		& ((1 << (grub_bfs_to_cpu32 (sb->log2_bsize)
 			  + DOUBLE_INDIRECT_SHIFT)) - 1));
